To start going with FastAPIs we should follow the following steps
1. Create Virtual Environment (python -m venv environment-name)
2. activate the created environment (environment-name/Scripts/activate)
3. Install required libraries (pip install library-name1 library-name2 library-name3 etc)
4. Start and run the server (uvicorn main:app -- reload)

we can use Path to enhance our readability
first import --> (from fastapi import Path)
use it like (def patient_view(patient_id: str = Path (..., description="ID of the Patient",example="p1")):


                    Https requests response codes with description
1. 2xx --> means Success
2. 3xx --> means redirection (further actions required)
3. 4xx --> means client side error
4. 5xx --> means server side error

200 (ok)          --> for get and post requests
201 (created)     --> for put request (something updated)
204 (not content) --> for delete request

400 (bad request)  --> something missing in fields
401 (unauthorized) --> login required
403 (forbidden)    --> logged in but access not permitted
404 (not found)    --> not exist

500 (internal server error) --> something broke in server 
502 (bad gateway)
503 (service unavailable)

                    HttpException Errors
from fastapi import HTTPException
